## 1. Objective restatement (traceability)

Produce two frozen artifacts and their harness:

1. `sakg/schema/envelope.schema.json` — JSON Schema **draft 2020-12** covering **every §4.2
   field** (17: 13 top-level + 4 nested under `provenance`), in three `$defs` profiles
   (`envelope_base`, `authored_node`, `stored_node`), with rules R1–R16.
2. `tests/sakg/fixtures/envelope/{valid,invalid}/*.json` exercising **every field, every
   status value, and every §4.2 invariant violation** — authored confidence, frequency-based
   promotion, deleted node.

**Acceptance (verbatim from `backlog/SAKG-1-backlog.yaml` L104–108; a node is `verified`
only when every command exits 0):**

```
uv run python -c "import json,pathlib;json.loads(pathlib.Path('sakg/schema/envelope.schema.json').read_text())"
uv run pytest tests/sakg/test_envelope_schema.py -q
test $(ls tests/sakg/fixtures/envelope/valid/*.json | wc -l) -ge 12
test $(ls tests/sakg/fixtures/envelope/invalid/*.json | wc -l) -ge 8
```

Expected margins at completion (design §10): **14 valid, 19 invalid**, 8 test functions with
T2/T3 parametrised to 33 test ids.

This restates design §§2, 5, 6, 11 without adding, relaxing, or reinterpreting any
requirement. **No requirement in this plan originates here**; every one carries a design or
backlog reference.

